<BaseLayout title="About · Santiago Madriz">
  <header class="page-intro" data-reveal><div class="eyebrow">About</div><h1>An engineer shaped by <em>quality, curiosity, and production reality.</em></h1><p>I work across software development and quality engineering, with a particular interest in systems that are clear to maintain, meaningful to test, and ready to operate.</p></header>
  <article class="prose" data-reveal>
    <h2>The throughline</h2><p>Quality Engineering taught me to look beyond whether software works once. I care about how it fails, how a team can change it safely, what feedback a pipeline provides, and whether production behavior is visible.</p>
    <p>That perspective naturally extends into broader software engineering: designing APIs, shaping data boundaries, building user experiences, documenting tradeoffs, and owning delivery rather than handing quality off at the end.</p>
    <h2>What I bring</h2><p>Hands-on automation, a risk-based testing mindset, frontend and backend fluency, CI/CD experience, and an instinct for turning unclear behavior into explicit contracts.</p>
    <h2>Outside engineering</h2><p>I also work in photography and audiovisual production in Costa Rica. Creative work has strengthened the same skills I value in software: observation, iteration, communication, and care for the final experience.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
